quran[42]{c,v,t}:
  80,1,"He looked displeased and turned (his attention) away,"
  80,2,because the blind man came to him (interrupting his discourse).
  80,3,"What would make you realise? Perhaps he would purify himself (by your attention),"
  80,4,or he would become mindful so that the reminder would benefit him.
  80,5,"As for the one who considers himself beyond need (of faith),"
  80,6,"you attend to him earnestly (to make him embrace Islam),"
  80,7,but you are not responsible if he does not purify himself.
  80,8,"As for the one who came to you striving,"
  80,9,"while he feared (his Lord),"
  80,10,you were inattentive to him.
  80,11,"No, indeed! These (verses of the Qur’an) are a Reminder."
  80,12,So let anyone who wishes remember it.
  80,13,"(It is written) in honoured scriptures,"
  80,14,"highly esteemed (and) purified,"
  80,15,"by the hands of angel scribes,"
  80,16,honourable (and) virtuous.
  80,17,Perish (the disbelieving) human! How ungrateful he is!
  80,18,From what substance has He created him?
  80,19,"He has created him from a fertilised egg (i.e. a zygote*), then proportioned him (during his development until the prenatal stage)."
  80,20,Then He made the way easy for him (to come out of the mother’s womb).
  80,21,"Then (at the end of his life span), He caused him to die and buried him."
  80,22,"Then, whenever He wills, He will resurrect him."
  80,23,But no! He (the disobedient man) has not yet accomplished what He commanded him.
  80,24,Then let human being consider his food:
  80,25,"How We poured down water in abundance,"
  80,26,"then, We split the earth, tearing (it) asunder,"
  80,27,"and cause grains to grow in it,"
  80,28,"and grapes and fresh vegetables,"
  80,29,"and olives and date palms,"
  80,30,"and gardens, densely planted,"
  80,31,"and fruits and (animals’) fodder,"
  80,32,as a sustenance for you and your livestock.
  80,33,"So, when the Deafening Blast comes,"
  80,34,"the Day when a man flees from his brother,"
  80,35,"and his mother and his father,"
  80,36,"and his spouse and his children,"
  80,37,"on that Day, every person will have such a (stressful) matter that it will make him unconcerned (with everyone else)."
  80,38,"(Some) faces, on that Day, will be shining,"
  80,39,laughing (and) rejoicing.
  80,40,"As for (some) faces, there shall be staining dust upon them that Day,"
  80,41,(and) darkness will overcast them.
  80,42,"These are the disbelievers, the wicked evildoers."
